    "narrative": "Our strongest plays for today\u2019s slate center on **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Corbin Carroll** (76.33), both of whom benefit significantly from high-upside matchups against mediocre arms. **Vinnie Pasquantino** leverages a stellar 18% SP skill boost against Spencer Arrighetti, further bolstered by a favorable 14% dynamic platoon edge. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start despite a slight drag from the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time; his profile as an elite speed threat is invaluable for our category scarcity needs, and he projects to maximize his production hitting in the #2 hole against Landen Roupp. **Mickey Moniak** (72.87) rounds out our core trio, taking advantage of a plus-matchup against Jake Irvin where his platoon splits provide the necessary floor to justify a strong start designation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the marginal inclusion of **Jose Caballero** (52.47) and **Isaac Paredes** (54.49). While **Isaac Paredes** faces the stiffest test of the day against Gerrit Cole, his platoon efficiency narrowly kept him above the bench threshold. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** carries risk due to a negative order adjustment, yet we are holding him in the lineup to hedge against potential late-game defensive substitutions that could yield a stolen base opportunity. **Austin Riley** (45.70) remains in the UTIL slot by the skin of his teeth; despite facing an elite arm in Yoshinobu Yamamoto and enduring a -6% order penalty, his raw power profile makes him a safer bet for Roto efficiency than our depleted bench, which currently sees **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined on the IL.\n\nWe are operating with a heavy \"Lineup Pending\" caveat across the board, which introduces variance to our current scoring projections. Managers should monitor **Gabriel Moreno** closely; while he projects well at 60.61, his value is predicated on the assumed #3 spot. Any shift to the bottom of the order could plummet his efficiency score. We continue to manage our bench depth carefully with **Josh Naylor** also inactive today, leaving us little room for error if we see mid-day weather delays or late-scratch announcements. Ensure all eyes remain on the confirmed cards to verify these projected lineup positions before first pitch.",
